      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Temperature and salinity are the primary drivers of water density in the ocean, a principle known as thermohaline forcing. Warmer water and fresher water are less dense than colder, saltier water, creating distinct density layers. In the Puerto Rico Trench, these variations dictate the stratification of the water column, which is crucial for deep-sea current dynamics and biogeochemical processes.",
